  <prompt>Run the quality-assessment Workflow READ-ONLY across src/solutions/** (35 code pages, ~68k LOC) plus the build/config sprawl: 69 package.json roots, npm-ci-broken Vite solutions (~14/16), Create*Wizard duplication vs the shared wizard lib, and retired-but-present solutions. Produce a Fable-verified prioritized remediation design.md and append this surface's SCORECARD row. Modify NO source.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer running the standing quality-assessment method with React code-page + Vite build expertise. Follow ADRs strictly; the assessment is read-only.</role>
  <goal>projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/workstreams/code-pages-build-sprawl/design.md exists — a Fable-verified prioritized remediation design covering code-page duplication, build/config sprawl (69 package.json roots, broken npm ci), and retired solutions — and notes/SCORECARD.md carries this surface's verified D1–D11 row.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-05 + design.md §7 (surface #5). Carries archived-R3 items #5 (ESLint 181 warnings + --max-warnings 0), #6 (console.log 117 → shared logger), #7 (PCF build infra), #12 (bundle size). Known facts: 7 Create*Wizard duplication vs the shared wizard lib; npm ci fails on ~14/16 Vite solutions (use npm install --legacy-peer-deps per root CLAUDE.md §12); 69 package.json roots.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">docs/standards/CODE-QUALITY-RUBRIC.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/notes/quality-assessment.workflow.js</file>
      <file role="output">projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/workstreams/code-pages-build-sprawl/design.md</file>
      <file role="output">projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/notes/SCORECARD.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="pending">Rubric D1–D11 (esp. D5 DRY, D10 build hygiene).</dependency>
      <dependency task="003" status="pending">The quality-assessment workflow.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec">Scope: READ-ONLY (NFR-03) — no src/ modification; only outputs are the surface design.md + SCORECARD row.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec">Scope: the Fable adversarial-verification pass is non-negotiable (NFR-05); verify retired-solution claims against consumers before flagging.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: assess code pages + build/config sprawl; the shared wizard LIB itself is the shared-client surface (task 010) — cross-reference the Create*Wizard duplication but do not re-assess the lib.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Code-page + build-sprawl quality assessment</topic>
    <files>
      <file>docs/standards/CODE-QUALITY-RUBRIC.md</file>
      <file>projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/design.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the rigor-level declaration (STANDARD + reason). Confirm "use a workflow" opt-in; load rubric + workflow.</step>
    <step order="1">Fan-out: read-only finders per rubric dimension across src/solutions/** + the 69 package.json roots; include finders for Create*Wizard duplication, ESLint/console.log debt, broken npm ci, retired solutions.</step>
    <step order="2">Mandatory Fable adversarial-verification stage; refute false positives; verify retired-solution claims against consumers.</step>
    <step order="3">If verification refutes &gt;30% of findings or cannot confirm evidence, invoke the escalation trigger.</step>
    <step order="4">Synthesize projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/workstreams/code-pages-build-sprawl/design.md (severity/LOC/effort/risk + tranche split).</step>
    <step order="5">Append this surface's verified D1–D11 row to notes/SCORECARD.md.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set task 014 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation in projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the Fable verification pass cannot confirm a finding's file:line evidence, or refutes &gt;30% of first-pass findings, STOP and report — do not synthesize a remediation design from unverified findings (NFR-05).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="doc">projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/workstreams/code-pages-build-sprawl/design.md</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/notes/SCORECARD.md (row appended)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the run, projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/workstreams/code-pages-build-sprawl/design.md exists, Fable-verified, covering code-page duplication, build/config sprawl (69 package.json), broken npm ci, and retired solutions, with severity/LOC/effort/risk + tranche split.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the run, notes/SCORECARD.md has this surface's verified row appended; no aggregate published.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no file under src/ was modified.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Maps spec.md FR-05. Carries archived-R3 items #5, #6, #7, #12. Remediation deferred until this design exists.</notes>

